#: input:276 standard
msgid "Bonuses and penalties"
msgstr ""

#: input:277 standard
msgid ""
"Each military site gets a bonus or penalty for the relative size of its "
"conquer area and the relative strength of its garrison. Values above the "
"average of the possible values get a bonus, below it get a penalty."
msgstr ""

#: input:280 standard
msgid "The soldier bonus uses a logarithmic scale for the effective strength:"
msgstr ""

#: input:282 standard
msgid "soldier_bonus = (ln(garrison strength) - 3.5) / 10"
msgstr ""

#: input:283 standard
msgid "The average value of 3.5 is roughly:"
msgstr ""

#: input:284 standard
msgid "the strength of a castle full of rookies: ln(12 * 2.76)"
msgstr ""

#: input:285 standard
msgid "the strength of one very strong hero: ln(33.11)"
msgstr ""

#: input:286 standard
msgid "the geometric mean of one rookie and a castle full of heroes:"
msgstr ""

#: input:288 standard
msgid "Dividing by 10 clamps the result to -0.25…+0.25."
msgstr ""

#: input:289 standard
msgid ""
"The area bonus simply uses the conquer radius: area_bonus = (r - 9) / 12. "
"The median radius of 9 belongs to the stronger medium military sites. Again, "
"the results are between -0.25 and +0.25 for conquer radiuses from 6 to 12."
msgstr ""

#: input:292 standard
msgid ""
"There are also two kinds of penalties for military sites in the core area of "
"the player’s economy. The first one is applied to the soldier bonus of "
"military sites within 20 steps to a trainingsite, then the area bonus is "
"added and the other penalty is applied to the sum for military sites within "
"32 steps of your starting position."
msgstr ""

#: input:296 standard
msgid ""
"The penalties decrease linearly with the distance. You can look up the "
"actual calculation in helpers.lua in the add-on’s directory, because it "
"doesn’t fit here."
msgstr ""

#: input:318 standard
msgid ""
"The bonuses make sure that bigger military buildings are actually worth "
"their buildcost and time, so all military sites have their use just like in "
"real battle situations. Sites in the core area are penalised because it’s "
"much easier there to build and to send strong soldiers. Military sites near "
"trainingsites are also penalised because it’s much faster to fill them with "
"freshly trained heroes. Please note that old trainingsite positions are "
"remembered, so you can’t boost your score just by dismantling a trainingsite "
"after it has filled its neighbourhood with heroes."
msgstr ""

#: input:326 standard
msgid ""
"The goal of all this complexity is to not have a clear winning strategy, to "
"allow all players play in their own preferred style."
msgstr ""

